-- CONTROL for #1046 (re-verbed 2026-08-26, #1986 rung 2): byte-identical to main.mdk
-- except the ONE shared local lambda is split into TWO locals, each used at exactly one
-- receiver type.  That is the ONE flipped dimension -- shared two-type local vs. two
-- single-type locals -- and it is precisely the dimension main.mdk's pinned rejection
-- keys on.  `impl Speak Dog` is STILL METHOD-LESS here, so a green control proves the
-- rejection is about the two-type merge and NOT about method-less impls or arg-tag
-- dispatch in general.
--
-- ⚠️ WHAT THE HARNESS ACTUALLY ASSERTS HERE IS EXIT 0 AND NOTHING ELSE -- a control
-- carries no stdout pin.  Measured by hand at the re-verb, not asserted by the gate:
-- build-run exit 0, stdout `woof|meow` (the method-less `Dog` impl still reaches the
-- inherited default once each local is monomorphic).
import iface.{Speak(..), speak}
data Dog = Dog
data Cat = Cat
impl Speak Dog where              -- METHOD-LESS: inherits the default
impl Speak Cat where
  speak _ = "meow"
main =
  let f = v => speak v
  let g = w => speak w
  println (f Dog ++ "|" ++ g Cat)
